      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T16:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Julio: I analyzed the `av1_get_block_hash_value()` function and its caller. I think your justification for 4096 is correct, but it seems that this should read:\n\n```\n// Maximum number of subblocks per block\n// The biggest block size supported by AV1 is 128x128, and the smallest\n// subblockt size is 2x2, herefore there can be\n// a maximum of (128/2) * (128/2) subblocks per block: 64 * 64 \u003d 4096\n```\n\nI.e., it is not necessary to mention superblocks in this comment.",
      "revId": "3d87f166f520a9d10b8413d808ad26d6323cd6d2",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5677a09a_217053d6",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/hash.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T16:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good remark! So, there are actually three concepts at play:\n- The 2x2 subblocks\n- The block itself\n- Superblock: IntraBC block size is limited by the superblock size being used by the frame (64x64 or 128x128)\n\nIn this case, the number \"4096\" assumes that we\u0027re using 128x128 superblocks, because those are the largest ones available in AV1. This dimension limit is intrinsically placed by the superblock size.\n\nI do think your comment is good, and an improvement over mine. Maybe we\u0027ll be fine by omitting the \"superblock\" remark here, and just say the largest intraBC block size can be is 128x128.",
      "parentUuid": "ce013016_37f1171b",
      "revId": "3d87f166f520a9d10b8413d808ad26d6323cd6d2",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "648c463d_356363d8",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/hash.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T16:46:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another thing to clarify is that these buffers are also used for subblocks larger than 2x2. So It would be good to say the smallest subblock size is 2x2, otherwise it implies these buffers are only used with 2x2 subblocks.\n\nYou definitely understand this code at a deeper level, which is why you know max block size 128 is linked to the superblock size. I merely analyzed the code and saw that the max block size is the maximum value in this array:\n\n```\n// Width/height lookup tables in units of samples.\n// The Block_Width table in the spec (Section 9.3. Conversion tables).\nstatic const uint8_t block_size_wide[BLOCK_SIZES_ALL] \u003d {\n  4,  4,  8,  8,   8,   16, 16, 16, 32, 32, 32,\n  64, 64, 64, 128, 128, 4,  16, 8,  32, 16, 64\n};\n```",
      "parentUuid": "5677a09a_217053d6",
      "revId": "3d87f166f520a9d10b8413d808ad26d6323cd6d2",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
